at dc fandom 2021 we finally got another  look at suicide squad kill the justice  league the next game from the team  behind the batman arkham series  rocksteady studios here's everything you  need to know about the upcoming co-op  action game for more on suicide squad  and gotham knights make sure to like  this video and subscribe  confusingly suicide squad is going to be  a continuation of the arkham games while  wb montreal's gotham knights is set in a  completely different universe in the  latest suicide squad trailer that  debuted at dc fandom there were a bunch  of callbacks to the original arkham  games suicide squad takes place after  the events of arkham knight and  rocksteady co-founder and creative  director sefton hill has said that some  narrative threats established in that  trilogy will pick up in this game  even though the suicide squad was  introduced in arkham origins wb  montreal's oft maligned prequel in kill  the justice league brainiac has attacked  metropolis so task force x or suicide  squad leader amanda waller sends her  group of criminal misfits to the city to  take out the alpha target who is  revealed to be superman  under the mind controlled effects of  brainiac we also see green lantern flash  and wonder woman which accounts for four  of the founding members of the league  although we see a car with batman symbol  on it the dark knight doesn't actually  show up which makes sense because  canonically speaking he's supposed to be  dead  or at least that's what he wants the  world to think  the four playable members of the suicide  squad are harley quinn deadshot captain  boomerang and everyone's favorite king  shark harley quinn will sound familiar  to anyone who's played arkham city or  knight as voice actress tara strong is  reprising her role we last saw harley  getting locked up at the end of arkham  knight so it's possible that task force  x leader amanda waller sprung her for  this job the trailer does begin with a  trip to arkham asylum after all she gets  around with a grapple and has her  signature baseball bat in hand we've  also had a run run-in with deadshot in  the arkham games he was hired by hugo  strange in arkham city to assassinate  political targets inside the place and  there was a side mission where you  captured him he was arrested by gcpd and  then later freed but they kept his  equipment king shark also has a very  recognizable voice he's played by wwe  wrestler samoa joe suicide squad  mastermind amanda waller will be calling  the shots while waller did appear in  arkham origins and arkham origins  blackgate she's now being voiced by  deborah wilson who you might recognize  from jedi following order or telltale's  batman we also caught a look at what  looks like gizmo in the latest trailer  he's a tinkerer that usually has run-ins  with the teen titans but seems to be  appearing in suicide squad to act as a  sort of cue for the squad in terms of  enemies brainiac is the big bad we've  seen so far invading metropolis and  bending superman's will to his own  ironically this isn't exactly the first  time we've seen this play out in recent  games superman turned evil in the first  injustice and in the sequel everyone  teamed up against brainiac we've also  caught a glimpse of the flash and green  lantern who are clearly all under  brainiac's spell  however it seems like wonder woman may  have escaped the same fate as she can be  seen fighting superman in some blink and  you'll miss it moments the penguin also  seems to have some sort of run-in with  the squad but it's not clear yet if he  was a metropolis on business  or if the game takes us to gotham city  suicide squad can be played in four  player drop-in dropout online co-op if  you fancy playing it alone the other  members of the squad will be controlled  by ai and you can switch between them at  will as i mentioned earlier suicide  squad killed the justice league is being  made by rocksteady studios who are most  famous for the arkham games asylum city  knight and vr it's been a long time  since we've seen a new release from them  as arkham knight was in 2015 and vr  followed in 2016.  in terms of key developers working on  the game it looks like arkham director  sefton hill is on board as creative  director  suicide squad killed the justice league  will launch on pc xbox series x s and  playstation 5 in 2022  [Music]  you
 

